{"additions":106,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"Pressing `o` on an issue or PR ran `gh <entity> view --web`, which resolves the page through the GitHub API — spending (GraphQL) quota to open an address that is fully derivable. The URL is now built locally from the `origin` remote (`git@github.com:…`, `https://github.com/…`, `ssh://git@github.com/…` forms, unit-tested); non-github.com remotes keep the `gh … --web` fallback. No behaviour change beyond zero API usage and a faster open.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":4,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T07:02:13Z","deletions":18,"headRefName":"fix/open-url-no-gh","labels":[],"number":141,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdTw9A","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new URL parser misses valid `github.com` remote variants (e.g., `.git/` and `ssh://git@github.com:<port>/...`), which can produce incorrect URLs or unnecessarily fall back to API-using behavior.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR removes GitHub API usage when opening an issue/PR in the browser from the GitHub page by deriving the repository `owner/repo` (NWO) locally from the `origin` remote URL and constructing the `https://github.com/...` URL directly, with a fallback to `gh … --web` for non-`github.com` remotes.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add `origin_github_nwo()` + `parse_github_nwo()` to derive `owner/repo` from common `origin` URL formats without calling GitHub APIs.\n- Update `open_in_browser()` to open the constructed URL directly for `github.com` remotes, otherwise fall back to `gh … --web`.\n- Add unit tests for the remote URL parsing helper.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/github/domain/client.rs | Builds GitHub issue/PR URLs locally from the `origin` remote to avoid API calls; adds parsing + tests and updates browser-open behavior. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/github/domain/client.rs:323**\n* The unit test for `parse_github_nwo` currently doesn’t cover the `.git/` trailing-slash case or the `ssh://git@github.com:<port>/...` form. Adding these cases would prevent regressions in the URL parsing behavior this PR relies on to avoid API usage.\n```\n        for url in [\n            \"git@github.com:td72/vig\",\n            \"git@github.com:td72/vig.git\",\n            \"https://github.com/td72/vig\",\n            \"https://github.com/td72/vig.git\",\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 1/1 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:05:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a8c6272f804432bbc13e60adf77d4fba2b4b3c91"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdWV6g","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new origin parsing path has a couple of correctness edge cases (git exit status not checked; `.git/` trailing slash parsing) that can produce invalid URLs or cache incorrect results.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/github/domain/client.rs:78**\n* `parse_github_nwo` removes the optional `.git` suffix before trimming a trailing `/`. For remotes like `https://github.com/owner/repo.git/` (or `ssh://…/repo.git/`), this returns `owner/repo.git` and produces an invalid GitHub URL. Trim trailing `/` first, then strip `.git`.\n```\n    let rest = rest\n        .strip_suffix(\".git\")\n        .unwrap_or(rest)\n        .trim_end_matches('/');\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 1/1 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:11:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a8c6272f804432bbc13e60adf77d4fba2b4b3c91"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLddLYA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:27:29Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a8c6272f804432bbc13e60adf77d4fba2b4b3c91"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLddMFA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:27:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c2cdeedd0320eb291ec2d85d1e10e629356686b2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLddMsw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:27:32Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c2cdeedd0320eb291ec2d85d1e10e629356686b2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLddjew","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:28:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c2cdeedd0320eb291ec2d85d1e10e629356686b2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdedZA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c2cdeedd0320eb291ec2d85d1e10e629356686b2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdeiEw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe shared parser module is not wired into the module tree and the in-use parser in `client.rs` still mishandles common remote variants (e.g., `.git/` and `ssh://...:<port>/`), which can produce incorrect URLs.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (3)\n\n**src/github/domain/client.rs:323**\n* The new parser behavior (trailing `.git/`, ssh with explicit port, http form, leading/trailing whitespace) isn’t covered by the unit test in this file. Adding cases for these inputs will prevent regressions in the local URL-building path.\n**src/github/domain/client.rs:61**\n* `git remote get-url origin` can return a non-zero exit status while `Command::output()` still returns `Ok(Output)`. In that case we currently parse (and cache) whatever is in stdout, which can permanently disable the local URL path or cache a wrong value. Check `out.status.success()` before parsing so failure reliably falls back to `gh … --web`.\n```\n        let out = Command::new(\"git\")\n            .args([\"remote\", \"get-url\", \"origin\"])\n            .output()\n            .ok()\n            .filter(|o| o.status.success())?;\n```\n**src/github/domain/client.rs:73**\n* This `parse_github_nwo` still has the two parsing bugs called out previously: (1) `.git/` won’t have `.git` stripped because `strip_suffix(\".git\")` runs before trimming the trailing `/`, and (2) it doesn’t accept the `ssh://git@github.com:<port>/owner/repo` form mentioned in the PR description. This can generate incorrect browser URLs for common remotes.\n```\n/// The URL is built locally from the origin remote — pressing `o` must not\n/// spend an API request. Non-github.com remotes fall back to `gh … --web`.\nfn open_in_browser(entity: &str, number: u64) -> Result<(), String> {\n    if let Some(nwo) = origin_github_nwo() {\n        let path = if entity == \"pr\" { \"pull\" } else { \"issues\" };\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 4/4 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:30:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"c2cdeedd0320eb291ec2d85d1e10e629356686b2"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdfq1g","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe behavioral change is small and test-covered, with only minor documentation cleanup suggested.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 4/4 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:32:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"bfec47fad6776f72d818ae83deb24b2c4efbf316"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLdh8uQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new shared remote parser should validate extracted components to prevent path traversal/invalid-path components being used in cache directory construction.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 4/4 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T07:38:11Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"cf9c838454e2ecb0375f4634c07e8f6fb6a27462"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:26Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33373536272/job/99429805291","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:33Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:36:13Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33369036302/job/99415725512","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:35:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:35:51Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33369036227/job/99415725591","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:35:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:36:31Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33369036302/job/99415725706","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:35:25Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:37:11Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33369036302/job/99415725616","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:35:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:37:11Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33369036302/job/99416142589","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:37:12Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:26Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33373536272/job/99429777661","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:26Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:36:10Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33369036227/job/99415725598","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:35:22Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T07:36:33Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33369036227/job/99415725329","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T07:35:23Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:26Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33373536272/job/99429816905","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-31T08:34:36Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"⚡ Open issues / PRs in the browser without an API request"}
